1. `handleForConnection()` is inside the `try`/`catch (\InvalidArgumentException)`, so any downstream middleware throwing one comes back out as `UnrecoverableMessageHandlingException`: no retry, straight to the failure transport. Messenger's own `InvalidArgumentException` extends `\InvalidArgumentException` too. `DbalConnectionsMiddlewareTrait` and `AbstractDoctrineMiddleware` both call the handler outside the `try`, please do the same.

2. The rename dropped the `@var list<string>` and the `@param list<string>|string ... or none to handle them all`. "Empty means all" is the one non-obvious bit of that API, please restore them.

3. I would make these two abstract classes rather than traits. The constructor is in the trait now, so a middleware needing an extra argument, `DoctrineOpenTransactionLoggerMiddleware` being the precedent with its `$logger`, has no `parent::__construct()` to call and must restate the whole constructor; miss the `$this->connectionNames =` line and you get `Typed property ...::$connectionNames must not be accessed before initialization` at runtime. Abstract classes give the same arity split, keep `parent::__construct()` working, and match `AbstractDoctrineMiddleware` right next door.

